Subject: [PATCH 02527/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A1
 (HEADLINE; oracle-distinct DETECTOR made ACTIONABLE;
 verifier_is_oracle=false) -- BiPRM BIDIRECTIONAL step-error LOCALIZATION +
 selective-prediction ABSTENTION (arXiv:2508.01682 VERIFIED 'Bidirectional
 Process Reward Model', the .404 SOTA-ingestion flagged_for_v405). .404
 (exp4375) PROVED the verifier ensemble DETECTS step-errors (AUROC 0.918, CI95
 lower 0.909, beats chance) on a corpus where SELECTION headroom is ~0
 (oracle@K==vote@1) -- but 'beats chance' is NOT a usable capability. This is
 the depth step: make the positive detector signal ACTIONABLE. (1)
 LOCALIZATION: run an L2R AND an R2L detector pass over the cached
 step-labeled FoVer corpus (the exp4375 corpus), FUSE the two scores (BiPRM
 bidirectional), and measure earliest-error-step localization
 (ProcessBench-style first-error accuracy/F1) for the bidirectional fusion vs
 a unidirectional L2R baseline. (2) ABSTENTION: from the detection score,
 report the selective-prediction operating point -- the accuracy-vs-coverage /
 risk-coverage curve, precision@high-recall, and the selective risk at a
 useful coverage (the 'I don't know' gate the detector spec named). (3)
 ONLINE-ACTOR HONESTY (the SOTA failure-mode): the R2L pass uses FUTURE
 context unavailable to an in-loop actor -> report bidirectional localization
 as an OFFLINE post-hoc detector, and keep a CAUSAL/L2R-only variant as the
 online-actionable number; NEVER conflate the two. Emit
 detector_localization_actionable BARE bool := (bidirectional fusion improves
 first-error localization over unidirectional L2R, CI95-excl-0, AND the
 risk-coverage curve yields a useful selective operating point).
 verifier_is_oracle=false (a learned/energy detection signal scored against
 cached candidates, oracle-distinct). A win = the oracle-distinct verifier
 graduates 'beats chance'->'localizes + abstains usefully'; a clean null (the
 unidirectional detector is already as good as bidirectional, or abstention
 gives no useful operating point) is decision-grade. Cached candidates, CPU,
 zero quota -- NOT hostage to any live LLM or the retired DiffusionGemma
 infra. NO TRM training.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
